Q: Different notation of returning inline struct in C23 A: <p>Anonymous <code>struct</code> and <code>union</code> are a <a href="https://www.cppreference.com/c/11" rel="nofollow noreferrer">feature of C11</a>. They are mostly useful when you have an anonymous <code>union</code> inside a <code>struct</code> or vice-versa.</p>
<p>For instance, I often use structures which are like “labeled unions,” with an anonymous union and sometimes anonymous structs:</p>
<pre><code>typedef enum {
    TYPE_1,
    TYPE_2,
} TheType;

typedef struct {
    TheType type;
    union {
        struct {
            int thing;
            char c;
        } forType1;
        struct {
            double type2_thing;
            char const * strForType2;
        };
    };
} TheLabeledUnion;

TheLabeledUnion lu[] = {
    { TYPE_1, .forType1 = { .thing = 5, .c = 'Z' } },
    { TYPE_2, .type2_thing = 8.9, .strForType2 = &quot;hey&quot; },
};
</code></pre>

